WEBVTT

00:07.270 --> 00:08.560
Good morning!

00:08.560 --> 00:09.660
Morning.

00:11.120 --> 00:12.730
Good morning.

00:15.030 --> 00:16.520
Don't be so clingy.

00:16.720 --> 00:17.730
Okay.

00:18.910 --> 00:20.060
See you later!

00:20.060 --> 00:21.130
Later.

00:21.130 --> 00:22.280
Have a nice day.

00:25.700 --> 00:30.780
Sorry. They're so relieved you 
came back, they can't stay away.

00:30.780 --> 00:32.530
Oh, I don't mind.

00:32.530 --> 00:38.310
It's a pleasant sort of weight,
 like paper secured by a paperweight.

00:40.990 --> 00:41.990
So...

00:42.560 --> 00:44.560
You're working today, right?

00:44.560 --> 00:45.950
Oh, yeah.

00:46.400 --> 00:48.610
I've got to turn in a rough draft.

00:49.030 --> 00:50.690
Of course.

00:51.570 --> 00:54.260
I'll finish up before the day is done.

00:55.330 --> 00:57.840
Want to go out somewhere tomorrow?

01:00.040 --> 01:02.170
<i>It'll be a date!</i>

01:04.440 --> 01:06.300
I look forward to it!

01:18.180 --> 01:25.480
Looks like it started before I knew it

01:26.230 --> 01:31.270
Thanks to you, I'm all smiles

01:33.190 --> 01:41.240
The usual townscape lends 
charm to the two of us

01:41.240 --> 01:46.750
Funny how it looks like a starry sky

01:50.500 --> 01:52.590
Suddenly buying flowers

01:52.590 --> 01:54.590
Standing around in the kitchen

01:54.590 --> 01:57.800
Sending a photo, because 
the setting sun is pretty

01:57.800 --> 02:02.350
Trying to spend as much 
time with you as I can

02:02.350 --> 02:05.350
This is all new for me

02:07.230 --> 02:12.900
I hope tomorrow is like today

02:13.230 --> 02:19.450
I've never felt this way before

02:19.450 --> 02:25.040
We'll go on a date this weekend if possible

02:25.700 --> 02:30.960
But it's fine if we stay home

02:32.210 --> 02:35.420
I can't wait to see you

02:38.010 --> 02:43.010
<b><b>Episode 12</b></b>

02:38.010 --> 02:43.010
<b><b>Fireworks with the Princess</b></b>

02:44.980 --> 02:47.030
<i>All I have are black dresses.</i>

02:47.650 --> 02:50.890
<i>This is our first date 
since annulling the pact.</i>

02:50.890 --> 02:53.020
<i>I want to make it one to remember!</i>

02:53.890 --> 02:56.230
<i>I need a new date outfit!</i>

03:00.850 --> 03:01.720
Huh?

03:02.960 --> 03:04.240
Shiori-san?

03:04.720 --> 03:05.530
Chibi-chan!

03:05.530 --> 03:06.910
Are you shopping?

03:07.150 --> 03:13.420
All the details about money and materials 
have me so dizzy, I don't know what's what.

03:14.570 --> 03:16.320
Where do you plan to wear the clothes?

03:16.660 --> 03:17.790
On a date.

03:17.790 --> 03:19.300
Oh, gotcha.

03:20.170 --> 03:21.930
Want me to help you?

03:22.430 --> 03:23.950
You'd be willing to?

03:29.670 --> 03:32.300
Dresses really seem like your thing.

03:32.520 --> 03:37.390
I just realized, this is my first time 
looking at clothes with a friend like this.

03:37.390 --> 03:38.670
It is?

03:43.150 --> 03:46.300
I wonder what kind of 
clothes Kuga-san likes.

03:46.300 --> 03:49.320
You seem like you'd wear what you 
want no matter what others think.

03:50.750 --> 03:57.090
W-Well, the past few days I've felt a 
growing urge to appeal to him more.

03:57.320 --> 04:02.080
There's no need for all that. I think 
Ichiro-kun would compliment any choice.

04:02.080 --> 04:04.960
I-I know that.

04:05.630 --> 04:08.170
It might've been the Shichi-Go-San festival.

04:08.170 --> 04:11.210
I forgot I'd chosen an orange kimono,

04:11.540 --> 04:15.600
and on the day of, I was crying because 
I wanted a light blue one instead.

04:15.600 --> 04:19.120
You know, you're like a flower 
amongst all this green.

04:20.200 --> 04:23.660
He hasn't changed at all since then.

04:24.050 --> 04:26.860
So different from all the other guys.

04:29.370 --> 04:32.010
I mean he's really nice, that's all!

04:32.010 --> 04:34.370
It doesn't mean anything, 
and he's my cousin anyway!

04:35.990 --> 04:38.670
Things just got kind of weird, huh?!

04:38.670 --> 04:39.890
Chibi-chan, are you—

04:40.160 --> 04:41.520
Wait, wait!

04:41.520 --> 04:43.410
Um...

04:43.880 --> 04:45.370
I-I love him.

04:46.870 --> 04:49.980
But as if he's my brother and then some.

04:49.980 --> 04:53.400
With a longing for it 
to go even beyond that.

04:53.610 --> 04:59.020
He's a bit older, and kind, and it was 
just convenient to fall in love with him.

04:59.810 --> 05:03.400
Ichiro-kun is never going 
to fall in love with me,

05:03.400 --> 05:05.880
so that actually leaves me free to love him.

05:06.530 --> 05:08.750
You're incredible, Chibi-chan.

05:08.750 --> 05:11.510
You know exactly what 
shape your feelings take.

05:11.850 --> 05:16.760
That's why I was actually relieved 
when he starting going out with you.

05:17.870 --> 05:19.030
This is the truth.

05:19.620 --> 05:21.290
I'm glad it was you.

05:21.290 --> 05:25.660
I-I swear to cherish this love!

05:25.660 --> 05:27.290
You're swearing it to <i>me?</i>

05:27.290 --> 05:29.390
Oh, enough already!

05:29.390 --> 05:30.550
On to the next store!

05:30.760 --> 05:31.760
Okay!

05:36.720 --> 05:38.180
All done!

05:38.180 --> 05:39.440
I'm home.

05:42.610 --> 05:45.350
Welcome home. You two were together?

05:45.350 --> 05:46.570
We went shopping.

05:46.570 --> 05:50.910
I was getting things together to 
look nice for tomorrow's date.

05:50.910 --> 05:54.840
I'm really going all out, 
so I hope you look forward to it!

05:56.820 --> 05:59.210
Hey, you go and tell him <i>that?</i>

05:59.210 --> 06:00.850
I'm just so happy!

06:02.200 --> 06:03.710
<i>Uh oh!</i>

06:04.380 --> 06:06.480
Machi, I gotta go out for a bit!

06:06.480 --> 06:08.100
Where are you going?

06:08.100 --> 06:09.980
Ichiro, let's play.

06:09.980 --> 06:12.590
To Sano-kun's place. I'll be right back!

06:12.970 --> 06:14.470
Aww...

06:14.470 --> 06:16.660
Want to play with me?

06:20.730 --> 06:23.240
Help you? With what?

06:23.690 --> 06:27.890
Teach me how to put more 
work into my appearance!

06:28.350 --> 06:32.730
<i>This is how Kuga-san turns out 
once he has a girlfriend?</i>

06:34.260 --> 06:37.400
Put together something promising 
with clothes you have on hand.

06:37.400 --> 06:40.240
Shall we see what we can do 
with your hair and eyebrows?

06:41.050 --> 06:42.240
Thank you!

06:44.450 --> 06:47.140
<i>He seems way more driven than usual.</i>

06:51.540 --> 06:54.250
<i>I can say, "I only just got here!"</i>

06:54.250 --> 06:55.380
Goshiki-san!

06:56.110 --> 06:57.260
Yes?

07:02.970 --> 07:04.400
<i>So cute!</i>

07:14.920 --> 07:16.160
Do I look weird?

07:20.410 --> 07:22.470
No, it's just...

07:22.470 --> 07:26.470
You look so lovely today, 
I'm the one who's surprised.

07:26.470 --> 07:27.660
Really?

07:28.920 --> 07:32.050
You look totally cute yourself.

07:37.560 --> 07:39.910
<i>This is bliss!</i>

07:39.910 --> 07:42.070
<i>I'm glad I put in the effort!</i>

07:44.620 --> 07:45.720
<i>His hand...</i>

07:52.370 --> 07:54.670
Sorry. My palm's all sweaty.

07:54.670 --> 07:56.920
I get it, I get it!

07:56.920 --> 07:59.010
It's kind of warm today.

08:03.020 --> 08:04.820
This is skating?

08:04.820 --> 08:06.420
I want to try it.

08:06.420 --> 08:08.360
I've never done it either.

08:08.740 --> 08:09.920
Let's give it a go.

08:16.720 --> 08:18.670
This is difficult.

08:19.120 --> 08:20.340
I can't stand up.

08:20.700 --> 08:23.360
<i>This is no time for holding hands.</i>

08:23.360 --> 08:26.000
<i>One of us needs to improve in a hurry.</i>

08:29.230 --> 08:30.860
Oh, wow!

08:31.140 --> 08:34.360
You can already skate that well?

08:36.460 --> 08:40.880
All I had to do was think of the frozen 
ground showdown in <i>Master of the Lion's Fist</i>.

08:40.880 --> 08:43.370
Moka-nee would be happy to hear that.

08:44.240 --> 08:47.120
I still can't walk without support.

08:49.170 --> 08:50.790
I'll be that support.

08:51.240 --> 08:54.830
No, you'll be in danger if I fall.

08:54.830 --> 08:57.140
I'll get the hang of this 
a little more first.

08:57.420 --> 08:59.630
O-Oh, okay.

09:07.870 --> 09:08.990
Here goes!

09:08.180 --> 09:09.470
<i>Lucky them.</i>

09:09.770 --> 09:13.000
<i>I'd be okay falling with him.</i>

09:13.670 --> 09:17.110
...it was just convenient to 
fall in love with him.

09:17.470 --> 09:19.700
<i>It was probably the same for me.</i>

09:20.480 --> 09:25.120
<i>First I had an ideal, and I chased the 
joy of being able to experience it.</i>

09:22.270 --> 09:23.990
Woop.

09:25.400 --> 09:26.800
<i>But now...</i>

09:29.290 --> 09:30.420
<i>You can do it!</i>

09:34.130 --> 09:35.620
Thanks for waiting.

09:40.620 --> 09:41.630
What's wrong?

09:42.000 --> 09:45.130
The night before the pact annulment,

09:45.730 --> 09:51.010
I couldn't sleep because I was 
thinking this love might end.

09:52.770 --> 09:56.960
And I was thinking,
 I wish I had told you more.

09:56.960 --> 09:58.040
Right.

09:58.380 --> 10:03.700
But I think in the end, unable to say more, 
I'd still have done the same things.

10:04.390 --> 10:07.230
I wanted you to be freed.

10:08.050 --> 10:13.420
I never thought I'd choose to 
let you go <i>because</i> I love you.

10:13.750 --> 10:16.610
Even if I had fallen in 
love because of the pact,

10:16.610 --> 10:19.630
I think I'd fall in love 
with you all over again.

10:19.630 --> 10:20.560
Oh, my!

10:20.560 --> 10:25.180
Sorry I was too stubborn 
to hold your hand earlier.

10:27.040 --> 10:31.550
I was thinking, with the pact gone, 
I need to be even more careful.

10:32.150 --> 10:34.310
Or levelheaded, or something.

10:35.020 --> 10:36.310
Why?

10:36.620 --> 10:39.550
I didn't want you to dislike me
 for getting carried away.

10:39.550 --> 10:41.940
Because it was already 
at risk of ending once.

10:42.640 --> 10:43.950
That won't happen.

10:44.420 --> 10:48.330
That's why I want to keep doing this.

10:48.560 --> 10:49.380
This?

10:50.750 --> 10:52.060
Letting you know things.

10:52.840 --> 10:55.370
I want to hold your hand.

10:57.110 --> 10:58.000
Sure!

11:12.070 --> 11:13.290
I'm home!

11:15.520 --> 11:16.820
Welcome home!

11:16.820 --> 11:17.740
Home.

11:18.370 --> 11:19.740
We're back.

11:21.000 --> 11:24.440
I bet you're hungry, huh? Let's eat soon.

11:24.440 --> 11:27.000
We picked up some yummy food.

11:27.860 --> 11:29.630
My muscles are aching.

11:29.630 --> 11:31.280
You worked <i>too</i> hard at it.

11:31.280 --> 11:32.880
Ow, ow.

11:34.720 --> 11:36.910
Goshiki-san, why aren't <i>you</i> in pain?

11:41.960 --> 11:44.520
We had <i>too</i> much fun last month.

11:45.240 --> 11:49.640
I spent more than I realized 
at New Years and on the trip.

11:50.020 --> 11:52.890
We've gotta cut back on spending this month!

11:52.890 --> 11:55.060
He looks busy.

11:55.760 --> 11:56.970
Ichiro.

11:57.400 --> 11:59.160
You guys are home?

11:59.560 --> 12:02.120
We're going to go play at the park.

12:02.120 --> 12:02.910
Both of you?

12:03.990 --> 12:06.650
Yuina-chan, Sakura-chan, 
and Ren-kun will be there.

12:07.020 --> 12:09.160
Okay, be careful.

12:09.610 --> 12:10.620
We will.

12:11.650 --> 12:13.050
Wait up!

12:17.080 --> 12:19.660
Huh? Looks like rain, doesn't it?

12:22.050 --> 12:23.720
Want to play at my place, then?

12:23.720 --> 12:26.180
Can we? I want to go, Yuina-chan!

12:27.400 --> 12:29.170
I might head home.

12:29.460 --> 12:33.050
Oh, Fumio-kun can come too, 
of course. Let's all go.

12:33.400 --> 12:35.060
Um...

12:35.380 --> 12:38.890
You didn't get to go skiing 
that time either, Machi-chan.

12:38.890 --> 12:42.490
Did you ask your family if you can 
go on the amusement park trip?

12:44.980 --> 12:46.440
Well, it's okay.

12:46.720 --> 12:48.490
Yeah, sorry.

12:49.670 --> 12:50.840
See you!

12:50.840 --> 12:52.200
Bye-bye!

12:53.250 --> 12:54.390
Let's go.

12:55.830 --> 13:00.390
<i>I happened to be passing by,
 but something's up with Machi-chan.</i>

13:01.940 --> 13:03.180
We're home.

13:05.870 --> 13:07.830
That was quick.

13:08.170 --> 13:10.850
It looks like rain, so we called it a day.

13:11.280 --> 13:12.850
Weren't you doing laundry?

13:12.850 --> 13:15.340
Oh, yeah! I'd better bring it in.

13:15.630 --> 13:17.500
Oh, I'll do it.

13:17.500 --> 13:18.730
It's no problem.

13:22.750 --> 13:23.850
I'm home.

13:25.620 --> 13:27.360
You were watching, Shio-chan?

13:28.250 --> 13:29.860
Uh...

13:30.550 --> 13:31.870
You were listening?

13:32.730 --> 13:34.740
Yes, just a little.

13:35.030 --> 13:36.610
Don't tell Ichiro.

13:37.060 --> 13:41.740
It's out of character for me to
 turn down my friends, you might say.

13:41.740 --> 13:43.090
Character?

13:43.090 --> 13:47.140
Are you saying you're unexpectedly shy?

13:47.800 --> 13:49.650
Just promise me!

13:53.370 --> 13:54.730
Machi-chan...

13:55.020 --> 13:55.790
Dog!

13:57.400 --> 13:59.340
Fumio, you're good!

14:00.420 --> 14:01.680
Want to go again?

14:02.600 --> 14:04.050
Ichiro should play, too.

14:04.050 --> 14:05.030
No, no!

14:05.930 --> 14:07.750
Didn't he look busy?

14:08.650 --> 14:11.090
Come on. Let's get something to drink.

14:12.590 --> 14:16.060
<i>In the end, it didn't rain anyway.</i>

14:18.920 --> 14:21.520
<i>The way Machi-chan was with her friends...</i>

14:21.520 --> 14:22.450
<i>Hold on.</i>

14:23.020 --> 14:25.460
<i>Is there some trouble between them?!</i>

14:28.280 --> 14:29.300
It's good.

14:33.150 --> 14:34.290
What's up?

14:35.510 --> 14:38.320
I'll keep your secret, but...

14:40.630 --> 14:44.810
It makes me sad to think something 
might be distressing you.

14:45.070 --> 14:47.080
I-I'm not distressed!

14:47.080 --> 14:50.320
It's just, out there they 
know me as being all cool.

14:50.320 --> 14:51.580
But...

14:51.580 --> 14:55.660
Oh. Do you think I didn't go play 
because we don't get along?

14:55.660 --> 14:57.080
W-Well...

14:57.080 --> 14:58.620
Not at all!

14:58.620 --> 15:01.570
They're all good kids, so everything's fine!

15:01.570 --> 15:04.320
More like, I'm not big on going 
to other peoples' houses.

15:05.100 --> 15:07.420
And it's more fun playing with Fumio.

15:07.850 --> 15:09.080
Right, Fumio?

15:13.450 --> 15:17.350
I'll play with Shio-chan. 
Machi, you can go over.

15:22.580 --> 15:26.240
Why would you say a thing like that?!

15:32.710 --> 15:34.730
I just felt a chill.

15:38.570 --> 15:40.130
Kuga-san.

15:40.130 --> 15:42.610
Wh-Wh-What happened?!

15:43.830 --> 15:45.120
I see.

15:45.480 --> 15:48.800
You were invited to go play, 
but you turned them down.

15:49.560 --> 15:54.840
Fumio, you thought Machi could 
go play if you stayed behind?

15:57.220 --> 16:02.320
Machi, did you turn it down 
out of consideration for me?

16:02.320 --> 16:05.160
I-It wasn't for your sake.

16:05.920 --> 16:08.150
It's because I like playing with Fumio.

16:08.420 --> 16:11.660
Yes, I know how fond you are of Fumio.

16:11.960 --> 16:14.140
I'm sorry, though.

16:14.620 --> 16:17.420
I meant it, it's not that!

16:17.420 --> 16:18.850
I mean, you...

16:19.700 --> 16:23.240
Everything you do is for our sake!

16:23.240 --> 16:26.410
I can help out, too!

16:26.650 --> 16:30.790
I-I... really am hopeless.

16:30.790 --> 16:32.040
No, you're not!

16:32.470 --> 16:38.280
Well, I was trying my best not to 
make you and Fumio feel that way.

16:39.130 --> 16:44.400
But I must have seemed stretched so thin, 
you felt you had to deny yourself.

16:44.800 --> 16:46.830
Now, I kind of understand.

16:47.190 --> 16:52.390
I have someone else who's important in my life,
and it made me lose sight of what's going on.

16:53.200 --> 16:56.360
I must have made you and Fumio sad.

16:56.360 --> 16:59.330
We're not sad, we're happy!

16:59.940 --> 17:01.770
We love Shio-chan.

17:02.330 --> 17:03.610
Thank you.

17:04.210 --> 17:05.450
Hey, Machi.

17:06.740 --> 17:09.830
Next time you're worried, 
be sure to tell me.

17:10.370 --> 17:14.480
You know how with cake, I get 
a bigger piece than Fumio?

17:14.480 --> 17:18.710
This is the same. If you've got trouble, 
let me handle the biggest third.

17:19.060 --> 17:19.850
Sure.

17:22.900 --> 17:26.640
Then that means, my piece 
is bigger than Fumio's.

17:26.640 --> 17:28.310
Uh, well...

17:30.290 --> 17:31.470
Fumio.

17:34.940 --> 17:36.620
Sorry I started crying.

17:38.310 --> 17:39.480
It's okay.

17:40.940 --> 17:45.010
What kind of playtime have 
you been turning down?

17:45.550 --> 17:51.170
Let's see, with going over to someone's house, 
getting permission seems like a pain.

17:51.170 --> 17:52.090
And then there's...

17:52.090 --> 17:53.040
Fireworks.

17:53.410 --> 17:56.750
Huh? You mean at the summer festival?

17:59.200 --> 18:04.380
<i>I had to work that day, and they were saying 
the view from the apartment was bad.</i>

18:05.070 --> 18:06.890
<i>I didn't know she'd been invited to go.</i>

18:07.250 --> 18:09.980
Summer festival, fireworks!

18:09.980 --> 18:10.910
That's lovely!

18:11.400 --> 18:14.620
Let's take part next time. I want to go, too.

18:15.520 --> 18:16.660
Let's go next time.

18:16.970 --> 18:18.370
Listen.

18:18.370 --> 18:21.160
Why don't we have a festival right away?

18:27.280 --> 18:30.280
A festival? I want in!

18:30.630 --> 18:32.340
Momoka-san's on board.

18:32.340 --> 18:33.650
Yeah!

18:33.650 --> 18:35.470
Let's invite Sano-san, too!

18:35.470 --> 18:36.790
Yeah!

18:40.300 --> 18:44.140
So we're having a summer 
festival in the winter, huh?

18:44.140 --> 18:46.060
Yeah, well...

18:46.060 --> 18:49.310
It's just us eating fried noodles outside 
and setting off fireworks, though.

18:49.310 --> 18:51.270
It's a Shiori-san thing to do.

18:51.860 --> 18:53.250
Hello.

18:53.250 --> 18:54.560
'Sup?

18:54.560 --> 18:55.570
Welcome.

18:55.840 --> 18:57.440
We brought fireworks!

18:56.070 --> 18:57.440
Fireworks Set

18:56.070 --> 18:57.440
Fireworks Set

18:56.070 --> 18:57.440
6 types of
handheld fireworks

18:57.440 --> 18:59.690
Thanks! You too, Sano-kun.

19:00.020 --> 19:02.690
I was happy to be invited.

19:03.670 --> 19:06.090
A pool in winter? That's weird.

19:06.490 --> 19:07.820
Are we getting in?

19:07.820 --> 19:10.460
We're putting in water 
balloons, not you guys.

19:10.460 --> 19:11.340
Want to fish for them?

19:11.870 --> 19:13.340
I do!

19:13.640 --> 19:16.160
But it's cold, so let's add hot water.

19:16.160 --> 19:17.500
Cold...

19:17.500 --> 19:19.840
<i>Good, they're having fun.</i>

19:24.720 --> 19:26.840
The noodles are great!

19:27.140 --> 19:28.840
It <i>does</i> feel like a festival.

19:28.840 --> 19:30.680
Fumio! Isn't this fun?

19:30.680 --> 19:31.750
Yeah.

19:30.680 --> 19:32.340
Wow, what's all this?

19:31.750 --> 19:33.480
Way to go!

19:32.900 --> 19:35.350
Sorry to do this unannounced!

19:35.350 --> 19:36.480
That's okay.

19:36.480 --> 19:37.870
Honami-san!

19:38.180 --> 19:40.580
We're holding a wintertime summer festival.

19:40.580 --> 19:42.360
Care to join us?

19:42.360 --> 19:45.900
If you say so, Goshiki-chan, I just might.

19:47.140 --> 19:49.540
When did you two get so close?

19:49.540 --> 19:51.750
We met up by chance in 
the middle of the night,

19:51.750 --> 19:53.780
and she taught me how to do my nails.

19:53.780 --> 19:58.490
She has such delicate, lovely skills, 
and she's really nice.

20:00.520 --> 20:01.690
Shio-chan!

20:01.690 --> 20:02.840
Coming!

20:04.690 --> 20:06.000
<i>So...</i>

20:06.000 --> 20:08.370
Shio-chan, do you know 
how to fish with this?

20:06.840 --> 20:09.750
<i>Goshiki-san is the one who was set free.</i>

20:08.370 --> 20:09.480
Oh, neat!

20:10.350 --> 20:13.850
<i>I never could have held 
this festival myself.</i>

20:13.850 --> 20:14.950
Ichiro!

20:16.080 --> 20:17.290
Fireworks.

20:17.290 --> 20:18.400
Let's go.

20:24.300 --> 20:25.470
Thank you.

20:26.320 --> 20:27.280
For what?

20:27.620 --> 20:30.380
"For what?" For every day.

20:31.140 --> 20:34.780
From "good morning" to the next 
"good morning." Every day.

21:17.800 --> 21:19.340
This was so much fun.

21:19.340 --> 21:20.470
Oh, yeah.

21:21.040 --> 21:22.800
Thanks for today.

21:22.800 --> 21:24.950
And thank you.

21:24.950 --> 21:28.220
I'm happy you went along 
with my random idea.

21:28.570 --> 21:32.460
I never could have gotten things together 
for a festival like this myself.

21:33.530 --> 21:36.980
It took more than just me to make 
something like this a success.

21:38.300 --> 21:39.350
It's really true.

21:40.210 --> 21:43.890
There are people around me 
who are willing to help.

21:44.320 --> 21:47.300
I've realized a lot of things,
 thanks to you.

21:47.300 --> 21:51.300
I-I'm apparently the type
 to run wild with things.

21:51.300 --> 21:56.040
Your cautious nature 
balances that out perfectly.

21:56.360 --> 22:00.080
Goshiki-san, you can go anywhere 
you want on your own now.

22:00.080 --> 22:04.170
Keep on running wild. 
That really makes me happy.

22:05.170 --> 22:06.660
You're right.

22:06.660 --> 22:09.930
There are many places I want to go
 and things I want to do.

22:10.330 --> 22:16.070
I'll work hard and get to where
 I can support myself, and then...

22:16.770 --> 22:19.570
I want to be the one to propose to you!

22:24.970 --> 22:28.740
<i>Oh, man. I can't keep up.</i>

22:28.740 --> 22:29.700
All right.

22:30.700 --> 22:42.290
A red thread winding around our legs
(nearby)

22:36.960 --> 22:38.050
Congrats!

22:38.050 --> 22:39.100
Grats.

22:39.880 --> 22:41.280
Congrats!

22:41.910 --> 22:44.490
Thank you, everyone!

22:42.290 --> 22:53.430
Just as the tightly tied knot comes undone

22:44.490 --> 22:45.480
I'll do my best!

22:45.480 --> 22:47.390
Everyone, hey...

22:49.760 --> 22:51.180
Thank you!

22:53.430 --> 23:00.100
Maybe if our feelings come together

23:00.100 --> 23:07.030
We can be like this forever

23:07.030 --> 23:16.870
A tug on my arm, by the bond that was formed that day

23:16.870 --> 23:22.710
A little at a time, we've come closer together

23:22.710 --> 23:27.510
More smiles for us

23:27.510 --> 23:40.310
That place I first learned of, and the shops we'll visit again tomorrow

23:40.310 --> 23:46.280
They'll all be part of these lovely days

23:46.280 --> 23:52.110
Cherished all the way

23:52.110 --> 23:58.410
Looking forward to it, good night
